OL,3,GNEWSAWork starts on 'anchor' cancer
OL,4,Asupport centre
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man who lost his husband to cancer
OL,7,Fhas described a charity as his
OL,8,F"anchor", as work begins on a
OL,9,Fpurpose-built centre for people
OL,10,Faffected by the disease.
OL,12,FAs it celebrates 30 years operating,
OL,13,FMaggie's announced on Thursday it had
OL,14,Fstarted work on its new facility at the
OL,15,FCambridge Biomedical Campus, which is
OL,16,Fexpected to open in early 2028.
OL,18,FRoland Sore, 62, has been supported by
OL,19,Fthe charity for five years after his
OL,20,Fpartner Andrew was diagnosed with
OL,21,Fcancer which spread to his lungs and
OL,22,Fbecame incurable.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
